<item>
            <title>[ITEP-92375] Provide full lifecycle management of installed models (list, get, delete, persist)</title>
                <link>https://jira.devtools.intel.com/browse/ITEP-92375</link>
                <project id="99912" key="ITEP">EdgeSW</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Today &lt;tt&gt;model-download&lt;/tt&gt; keeps everything in memory (&lt;tt&gt;ModelManager._jobs&lt;/tt&gt;). After a restart the service does not know which models are installed; the only &quot;memory&quot; is the directory tree on the shared volume, but the API does not scan it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The only ways to get information about installed models today are:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;GET /api/v1/models/results&lt;/tt&gt; which iterates over in memory jobs and returns only models installed during the lifetime of the current process.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;GET /api/v1/models/jobs?model_name=...&lt;/tt&gt; which also reads in memory jobs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Both endpoints are tied to the job list, which is lost on every restart. There is also no API to delete a model; the consumer must delete files directly from the shared volume, which couples it tightly to the internal directory layout of &lt;tt&gt;model-download&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As a result, every consumer of &lt;tt&gt;model-download&lt;/tt&gt; has to maintain its own persistent registry of installed models on top of the service. An example of such a consumer side workaround is &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/open-edge-platform/edge-ai-libraries/blob/main/tools/visual-pipeline-and-platform-evaluation-tool/vippet/managers/model_manager.py&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;installed_models.json&lt;/a&gt; maintained on top of the service.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The goal is to make &lt;tt&gt;model-download&lt;/tt&gt; the single source of truth about installed models, so consumers do not need a parallel registry. This requires:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;A persistent registry of installed models that survives restarts.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Endpoints to list all installed models and to query a specific model.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;An endpoint to delete an installed model.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;(Optional) Persisting jobs across restarts as well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
</description>
