                <customfields>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            <customfield id="customfield_11609" key="com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.customfieldtypes:textarea">
                        <customfieldname>Acceptance Criteria</customfieldname>
                        <customfieldvalues>
                            <customfieldvalue>&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Persistent registry:
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Information about installed models is stored on a shared volume. A small JSON file or a small file based database (for example SQLite) is acceptable as a first step.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;On startup the service loads the registry and reconciles it with the actual contents of &lt;tt&gt;MODELS_DIR&lt;/tt&gt; (drops entries whose files no longer exist; optionally adds entries discovered on disk but missing in the registry).&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;The registry is updated atomically on every successful download, upload and delete.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;New endpoint &lt;tt&gt;GET /api/v1/models&lt;/tt&gt; that returns all installed models. For each model the response contains at least:
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;model name (as used when downloading)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;hub / source (huggingface, geti, ultralytics, omz, ...)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;model path on disk&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;precision(s) available&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;size on disk&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;installation timestamp&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;any plugin specific metadata that was returned at download time&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;models installed by &lt;tt&gt;POST /models/upload&lt;/tt&gt; are also listed&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;New endpoint &lt;tt&gt;GET /api/v1/models?name=&amp;lt;name&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt; (and/or &lt;tt&gt;GET /api/v1/models/&amp;lt;name&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt;):
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;returns the matching installed model(s) with the same shape as above&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;optional filters: &lt;tt&gt;hub&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;precision&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;if multiple matches exist (same name in different hubs or precisions), all of them are returned&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;returns 404 when no model matches&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;New endpoint &lt;tt&gt;DELETE /api/v1/models/&amp;lt;name&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt; (or &lt;tt&gt;DELETE /api/v1/models?name=...&amp;amp;hub=...&amp;amp;precision=...&lt;/tt&gt;):
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;optional filters: &lt;tt&gt;hub&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;precision&lt;/tt&gt;, so the caller can delete only one variant&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;removes all files that belong to the model from disk&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;removes the corresponding entry from the persistent registry&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;returns the list of removed paths in the response&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;returns 404 when the model does not exist&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;returns 409 if the model is currently being downloaded (active job for that model)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;path traversal protection: the resolved paths must stay inside &lt;tt&gt;MODELS_DIR&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;All read endpoints reflect the actual state on disk and survive a restart of the service.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;(Optional, lower priority) Persist jobs across restarts:
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;all jobs (&lt;tt&gt;download&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;convert&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;upload&lt;/tt&gt;) survive a restart&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;jobs that were &quot;running&quot; at the moment of the crash are marked as &lt;tt&gt;interrupted&lt;/tt&gt; (or &lt;tt&gt;failed&lt;/tt&gt;) on the next startup, not left as &lt;tt&gt;running&lt;/tt&gt; forever&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;the same storage backend as the model registry is reused&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</customfieldvalue>

                        </customfieldvalues>
